const body = `<h1>2.7b — Character Creator: Display</h1>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">RPG Build</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <h3>Part 3: printCharacterSheet() — Show Your Creation</h3>

    <p>
        Your character has stats but no way to display them. Build a method that
        prints a formatted character sheet to the console.
    </p>

    <p><strong>Requirements:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Method signature: <code>public void printCharacterSheet()</code></li>
        <li>Print the character's name, HP bar, and six stats</li>
        <li>Use <code>System.out.println()</code> to format each line</li>
        <li>The output must be clean and readable — think about spacing and alignment</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Sample output:</strong></p>
    <pre><code><span class="output">====================
== GROG THE MIGHTY ==
====================
HP: [████████░░] 20/20

STR: 15
DEX: 10
CON: 12
INT:  8
WIS: 11
CHA:  9
====================</span></code></pre>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic Checkpoint</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Where does <code>printCharacterSheet()</code> fit in the
                three-step pattern?</li>
            <li>The HP bar shows <code>hp</code> out of <code>maxHp</code>.
                What would happen if these two values get out of sync?</li>
            <li>You're printing six stats. What's repetitive about it?
                Can you imagine a way to clean this up? (We'll explore
                this with arrays in Unit 6.)</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="tinker">
        <h3>Tinker: The HP Bar</h3>
        <p>
            An HP bar shows filled and empty blocks. You need to figure out:
        </p>
        <ol>
            <li>How to calculate the number of filled blocks from <code>hp</code>
                and <code>maxHp</code>. (Think: what percent of HP is remaining?)</li>
            <li>How to build a String with that many filled characters (■) followed
                by empty characters (□) to make 10 total.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
            Be careful: you're dividing two integers. What does Java do with
            integer division? What order of operations do you need to avoid
            getting 0 blocks for every HP value less than maxHp?
        </p>
        <p>
            The <a href="../docs/unit-02/character-creator.html">Character Creator guide</a>
            has the formula if you get stuck — but try to derive it yourself first.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-02/character-creator.html">Student RPG Guide: Character Creator</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-02/string.html">String Methods</a> — formatting helpers</li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
